ITEMS=[]
def family(options,rows):
 assert len(options)==len(rows)==4
 for i,(q,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((q,[options[i]]+options[:i]+options[i+1:],e))
family(['The Registrar','The Designated Firearms Officer','The Appeal Board','The criminal court'],[
('Under the Act, which authority has the statutory power to issue firearm licences when the applicable requirements are met?','Section6 assigns issuing powers to the Registrar. Applications are commonly delivered through the relevant DFO.'),
('A resident must deliver a competency application to the official responsible for the area where the resident ordinarily lives. Which official is identified in section9?','The application is delivered to the relevant Designated Firearms Officer, rather than directly to an appeal body.'),
('An applicant challenges a refused competency application through the statutory appeal procedure. Which body may confirm, vary or reverse the challenged decision?','Section133 gives that function to the Appeal Board.'),
('A person is convicted of an offence listed in section103. Which body makes the relevant judicial determination concerning unfitness at conviction?','Section103 concerns the court\'s determination following conviction; it is distinct from the Registrar\'s section102process.')])
family(['A competency certificate','A licence for the particular firearm','Accreditation of an organisation','A temporary possession authorisation'],[
('A person has completed the required knowledge and practical training and seeks SAPS recognition of the relevant competence. Which document is being sought, before a separate firearm licence?','A competency certificate records the relevant competency. It does not itself replace a licence for an ordinary firearm.'),
('A competent applicant wants continuing authority to possess a specific ordinary firearm for an approved purpose. Which document directly concerns that particular firearm?','Section11 requires a separate licence for each firearm, although multiple licences may appear on one document.'),
('A sports-shooting organisation seeks official recognition under section8to perform its statutory association role. What status is it applying for?','Accreditation concerns the organisation\'s suitability and capacity for its statutory functions.'),
('The Registrar permits possession under section21for a specified period and subject to stated conditions. What kind of permission is this?','Section21 provides temporary authorisation, with its period and conditions determined by the Registrar.')])
family(['The ordinary age requirement','Citizenship or permanent residence','Fitness and suitability','Freedom from substance dependence'],[
('A first-time competency applicant has no approved exception and is only19on the day the DFO receives the application. Which section9requirement is not met?','The ordinary minimum is21on receipt by the DFO; the Registrar may allow an under21application for compelling reasons.'),
('A first-time applicant is neither a South African citizen nor a permanent resident. Which requirement for an ordinary competency certificate is at issue?','Section9(2)(b) requires South African citizenship or a permanent South African residence permit.'),
('An applicant meets the age and residence conditions but has a documented inclination to violence. Which suitability issue must still be considered?','Competency includes being fit and proper, of stable mental condition and not inclined to violence; age alone is insufficient.'),
('An applicant is dependent on a substance with an intoxicating effect, even though the application form is otherwise complete. Which specific section9condition is implicated?','Section9 requires that the applicant not be dependent on a substance with an intoxicating or narcotic effect.')])
family(['Evidence of legal knowledge','Evidence of practical competence','The prescribed fingerprint set','The relevant competency certificate'],[
('A first-time applicant has passed practical handling but has not completed the prescribed assessment of the Firearms Control Act. What training evidence is still missing?','Section9 separately requires successful completion of the prescribed knowledge assessment and practical training.'),
('A learner has demonstrated knowledge of the Act but has not completed the prescribed safe-handling training and practical assessment. What separate evidence remains necessary?','Legal knowledge does not replace the prescribed practical training and assessment required by section9.'),
('An ordinary individual application includes the completed form and required supporting information but omits the biometric material required by section6. What is missing?','Section6 requires the prescribed application, including a full set of the applicant\'s fingerprints.'),
('An individual applies for an ordinary firearm licence but has not obtained the SAPS competency document relevant to that firearm. Which prerequisite is absent?','Subject to the Act\'s specific provisions, section6prohibits issuing a licence without the relevant competency certificate.')])
family(['A natural person','A juristic person','A nominated responsible person','An accredited association'],[
('A private individual applies in their own name, rather than on behalf of a company or trust. Which legal description fits the applicant?','A natural person is an individual human being, distinguished from a juristic entity.'),
('A company wants a licence in connection with its lawful business and must nominate an individual to apply for it. What kind of applicant is the company?','Section7 addresses applications by juristic persons, which must act through a nominated natural person.'),
('A company\'s licence identifies the individual nominated to act for the company under section7. What statutory role does that individual hold?','The nominated individual is identified as the responsible person and is treated as the holder for the Act\'s purposes.'),
('A sports organisation has obtained the Registrar\'s recognition under section8and provides the statutory membership declaration for a dedicated applicant. What status describes the organisation?','The declaration comes from the appropriate accredited association, not merely any informal group.')])
family(['A licence condition','A regulation','A Gazette declaration','An application statement'],[
('A business firearm licence specifies the business purpose for which the firearm may be used. Which instrument contains that individual restriction?','Section20 requires the licence to specify its business purpose and limits use to that specified purpose.'),
('A generally applicable rule sets requirements for prescribed safe custody under powers granted by the Act. What type of subordinate rule is this?','The Act allows regulations to prescribe details such as safe-custody requirements.'),
('After the required consultation, the Minister formally designates premises as a firearm-free zone under section140. Which publication gives that designation its statutory form?','Section140 provides for a notice in the Gazette declaring premises or categories of premises firearm-free zones.'),
('An applicant supplies a personal residential address and declares the information in the prescribed form. What is this information part of?','It is information supplied in the application. Knowingly false or misleading application information is an offence.')])
family(['A reasonable opportunity to respond','Assistance from a legal representative','Examination of a called witness','Consideration of the relevant facts'],[
('Before a section102unfitness decision, a person must be allowed to explain why the declaration should not be made. Which procedural protection is directly involved?','Section102 requires a reasonable opportunity to advance reasons before the Registrar decides.'),
('A person appearing in a section102inquiry wants a lawyer to assist and speak on their behalf. Which entitlement applies?','Section102 expressly permits representation by a legal representative.'),
('A statement-maker is called to a section102inquiry. The affected person wants to question that witness through a lawyer. Which entitlement addresses this?','The person may examine the called witness or have the legal representative do so.'),
('The Registrar receives the affected person\'s explanation and supporting material before deciding a section102inquiry. What decision-making obligation applies?','The Registrar must duly consider the matter and relevant facts rather than treating the notice itself as the final decision.')])
family(['A threat involving a dangerous weapon','Failure to take prescribed safekeeping steps','False or misleading required information','A final protection order'],[
('Sworn information states that a person has expressed an intention to injure another person with a dangerous weapon. Which section102ground is directly raised?','Expressed intent to kill or injure oneself or another with a firearm or dangerous weapon can support the statutory inquiry.'),
('Evidence shows that an owner repeatedly leaves firearms unsecured contrary to the prescribed custody requirements. Which section102ground is directly raised?','Failure to take prescribed safekeeping steps is an express ground for considering unfitness.'),
('An owner knowingly supplied inaccurate information required under the Act. Which section102ground is directly raised by the dishonest information?','Providing false or misleading required information is a ground for the Registrar\'s unfitness process.'),
('A final order under the Domestic Violence Act has been issued against a firearm owner. Which section102ground is directly raised?','A final domestic-violence protection order is an express ground for the Registrar to consider unfitness through the required procedure.')])
family(['Refusal of an application','Cancellation of an existing licence','Cancellation of accreditation','A declaration of unfitness'],[
('The Registrar considers a new licence request and decides not to grant it. Which type of administrative decision has occurred?','Refusal concerns an application that has not been granted; it is distinct from cancelling an existing licence.'),
('After the required notice and consideration of representations, the Registrar ends an existing licence because its conditions were breached. Which decision is described?','Section28 allows cancellation of an existing licence on the stated grounds after the required process.'),
('An organisation no longer meets the suitability criteria for its section8recognition. After the statutory process, that recognition is withdrawn. Which decision is described?','This concerns cancellation of accreditation, rather than an individual firearm licence.'),
('After the section102procedure, the Registrar finds that a person is not fit to possess firearms. Which decision causes the broader section104consequences?','A declaration of unfitness affects all competency certificates, licences, permits and authorisations under section104.')])
family(['The licence remains valid pending the decision','The additional licence lapses on moving','The unfitness status continues during appeal','The permission applies only for its stated period'],[
('An owner lodges a complete licence-renewal application within the statutory period, but the Registrar has not decided it by the original expiry date. What does section24provide?','A renewal lodged within the required period keeps the licence valid until the application is decided.'),
('A person holds a section12additional licence based on living at the primary licence holder\'s premises, then moves elsewhere. What is the statutory consequence?','The additional licence lapses when that holder moves from the premises and must be returned forthwith.'),
('A person declared unfit under section102appeals the decision. Without any decision setting it aside, what is the status while the appeal is pending?','Section104 states that unfitness remains in effect pending finalisation of the appeal.'),
('A person relies on a section21authorisation whose document specifies a limited period. What determines the duration of that temporary permission?','The Registrar determines the period of a section21authorisation; it is not automatically the ordinary licence term.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==40
